1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From The New Mexican of Wednesday, June 6, 1973:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://searchapi.newspaperarchive.com/cache/50533290.pdf?forcedownload
2 CONT
2 CONT Origins of New Mexico Families by Fray Angelico Chavez:
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Manuel Roybal, son of Mariano Roybal, deceased, and Maria Loreta Velasquez, married Maria Josefa Quintana, May 13,1818, at El Rancho de San Ildefonso. Sometime after 1851, the family moved to the newly-settled Mora valley and
2 CONC  its environs, where Juan Manuel died on April 8, 1858.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their known sons were as follows: 
2 CONT *1. Jose Desiderio, born February 11,1821, who married Maria Dolores Alarid; 
2 CONT *2. the twins, Jose Monico and 
2 CONT *3. Jose Fernando, May 20, 1830; and 
2 CONT *4. Jose Candelario, February 5, 1837.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their known daughters were:
2 CONT *1. Ignacia, who married Jesus Trinidad Sandoval on November 7, 1836; 
2 CONT *2. Maria de Jesus, who married Jose Dolores Coca, November 6, 1843; 
2 CONT *3. Maria Guadalupe, born August 15,1825; 
2 CONT *4. Maria Dolores, January 9, 1828; and 
2 CONT *5. Ana Maria, October 21, 1832.
