1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Juan Cristobal Pacheco is my 3 gr granfather and he is mentioned in the book EL Centenario De La Palabra El Rito Presbyterian Church 1879-1979 Chacon New Mexico.  It is an account of Don Leandro Vasquez who tells o
2 CONC f the early families of the settlement.   Chacon was then called El Rito del Agua Negra.  Juan Cristobal lived in the area called Romeroville Colonia with Juan Duran, Juan Jose Vigil, Francisco Vasquez.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Cristobal Pacheco served in 1861 as a 1st Regiment New Mexico Volunteer Militia Infantry soldier company E  who served in organizations from the Territory of New Mexico/Fort Union and received his pension on Jan 14 1893.  Uni
2 CONC on Soldiers were paid about 10.00 a month Military records at Fold3.com
2 CONT
