1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dad born on Parkview New Mexico, he and his brothers worked the lumber mill  industry riding the rails to Colorado.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family moved to Albuquerqe early 1940 he met and married Lucy Salas my dear mother Louie my brother was born 1942. They moved to Los Angeles 1944 working in the shipyards for the war effort. lived on Grand near Angeks flight,
2 CONT
2 CONT Dad was hard working, family loving, God fearing man flawed loke the rest of us.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died before I was mature enough to really get to know him .
2 CONT
2 CONT We were not prepared for that, Below is something I wish would have said at his wake. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He went to Barber College mid fifties, he ingrained in me get educated. Go to work everyday, make sure people you work for get what they want and you will what you want, make as many friends as   possible , dont burn you bridges.
2 CONT  He was the glue for our families visiting, , his parents, our Aunts, Uncles  My moms family in New Mexico a tradition I have kept going.
2 CONT
2 CONT I look forward to seeing you in heaven.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==
