1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From The New Mexican of Wednesday, June 6, 1973:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://searchapi.newspaperarchive.com/cache/50533290.pdf?forcedownload
2 CONT
2 CONT Origins of New Mexico Families by Fray Angelico Chavez:
2 CONT
2 CONT Romualdo Roybal, son of Desiderio Roybal and Maria Dolores Alarid, married Maria Monica Gonzales on February 20,1873. His family was living at Los Fuertecitos, and the bride's at La Ciruelita., They later resided at the new town o
2 CONC f Santa Clara, later named "Wagon Mound," and also had a ranch at the nearby Canada de Tata Vegue. Their known children were:
2 CONT *1. Andres, November 23, 1873;
2 CONT *2. Eva, November 3, 1877, who married Jose Donato Herrera, October 3, 1892, and then Ricardo Martinez, January 20, 1901; 
2 CONT *3. Aurelia, July 23,1882, who married George M. King, November 4, 1899; 
2 CONT *4. Nicolasa, born at La Canada de Tata Vegue, November 29, 1884, who married Fabian Chavez (q.v.);
2 CONT *5. Vitoria, March 6, 1888, who married Agustin A. Sosaya, August 12, 1909; 
2 CONT *6. Tranquilino, April 13, 1891, who married Tena Lewis; and 
2 CONT *7. Romualdo, born December 15, 1895.
