2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 JUL 2003
2 PLAC Pueblo, Pueblo County, Colorado, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Lupe Apodaca - Pueblo Chieftain - July 23, 2003 - Lupe Apodaca, 90, a lifetime Puebloan, born April 19, 1913, passed away July 20, 2003, at the Life Care Center of Pueblo. Before her health began to fail her, Lupe was an active me
2 CONC mber of St. Mary Church. She was also the secretary of the former ladies club Sociedad Femenil de Proteccion Mutua. Preceded in death by her parents, Pedro Arguello and Julia Avila Morales; stepfather, Pedro Morales; two sisters, 
2 CONC Maclovia and Josephine Pludio; two brothers, Joe and Pedrito Arguello. She leaves to cherish her memory daughter, Connie (Korky) Kochendarfer; sister, Lucille Huerta; grandchildren, Debra (Joe) Friederich, Lawrence Maes, Annette (
2 CONC Vince) Tinajero; great-grandchildren, Natalie and Jammin Friederich, Jonelle and Little Vincent Tinajero; special cousin, Tim (Julia) Arguello; numerous other family members consisting of the Pulido family, Arguello family, Huerta
2 CONC  family and the Montoya family. Visitation, 9 a.m. until 5 p.m. today, Angelus Chapel. Both services St. Mary Catholic Church; Rosary vigil, 7 p.m. today, and funeral Mass, 10 a.m. Thursday. Interment, Roselawn Cemetery. Family wi
2 CONC ll receive friends at 1201 Jackson St. and the Zaragoza Hall following the burial rites.
