1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From her obituary, via Find A Grave:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://images.findagrave.com/photos/2018/169/161447818_1529420312.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Margarita Vigil:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Margarita Vigil, formerly of Trinidad, Nov. 27, 1975, at the Four Seasons Nursing Center. Predeceased by her husbands, 
2 CONT *Antonio Sanchez, Apr. 22, 1926, and 
2 CONT *Samuel Vigil, Sept. 6, 1967. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born May 31, 1882, in Mora County, New Mexico, living in Trinidad for 37 years before moving to Pueblo in 1973. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the mother of:
2 CONT *Mrs. Lucinda Moya, Santa Fe, NM
2 CONT *Mrs. Carlota Baca, Pueblo
2 CONT *Mrs. Julia Romero, Raton, NM
2 CONT *Joe T. Sanchez, Watrous, NM, and 
2 CONT *Gabriel Sanchez, Sr., of 2403 Winnipeg, where the family will receive friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the sister of:
2 CONT *Mrs. Senida Dominguez, Tucumcarri, NM
2 CONT *Mrs. Feloniz Lucero, Denver
2 CONT *Mrs. Amalia Archuleta, Watrous, NM
2 CONT *Mrs. Eloisa Lovato, Denver, and
2 CONT *Antonio Trujillo, La Junta.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thirty-nine grandchildren, numerous great- and great-great-grandchildren, and many nieces and nephews also survive. Recitation of the Rosaries 7 p.m. Saturday, Angelus Chapel, and 7 p.m. Sunday, Holy Family Church. Mass of Christi
2 CONC an Burial 9 a.m. Monday. Interment, Roselawn. Trinidad paper please copy.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
