1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From The Albuquerque Morning Journal, of Wednesday, June 25, 1919:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Miss Aurora Lucero is wed to Gardner D. White'''
2 CONT
2 CONT (Special Correspondence to Morning Journal) Santa Fe, June 24 - Miss Aurora Lucero, daughter of former Secretary of State Antonio Lucero, was married yesterday afternoon to Gardern D. White, of Denver, a young businessman, by Vica
2 CONC r General Antonio Fourchegu. Miss Julieta Lucero, sister of the bride, was bridesmaid, and David Torres of Santa Fe, was best man. The couple expects to leave shortly for South America, where the groom has business interests.
