1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the Santa Fe New Mexican of Sunday, Jan. 5, 1969:
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicolasa Chavez., 84, dies In Los Alamos
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicolasa Roybal de Chavez, 84, died Saturday in Los Alamos Medical Center.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a descendant from a long line of early Spanish sellers in New Mexico and was a direct descendant of Ignacio de Roybal y Torrado, who was born in Caldas de Reyes, Galicia, Spain, and came here with DeVargas for the reconque
2 CONC st of Santa Fe in 1693.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by 
2 CONT *sons 
2 CONT **Fra Angelico Chavez, priest-historian; 
2 CONT **Judge Rumaldo Chavez; 
2 CONT **Francisco E. Chavez, Los Alamos; 
2 CONT **Fabian Jr.; 
2 CONT **Judge Antonio E. Chavez, Los Angeles, and 
2 CONT **Jose A. C. Chavez, Santa Fe; 
2 CONT *daughters 
2 CONT **Mrs. Martha Matt, 
2 CONT **Mrs. Nora Chavez, 
2 CONT **Mrs. Adela Montoya of Los Angeles, 
2 CONT **Mrs. Consuela Gorski of Grosse Point Farms, (Michigan), and 
2 CONT **Mrs. Clara Gutierrez of Santa Fe; 
2 CONT *sisters 
2 CONT **Mrs Victoria Sosaya and 
2 CONT **Aurelia King, Santa Fe; 
2 CONT *brother, Tranquelino Roybal, Los Angeles, and 
2 CONT *32 grandchildren and two great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Chavez attended Highlands University in 1903 and was a teacher at Wagon Mound until her marriage lo Fabian Chavez Sr. in 1909. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of the Third Order of St. Francis and La Union Protectiva.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral arrangements are pending at Memorial Chapel in Santa Fe.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Las Cruces Sun-News of Sunday, Jan. 5, 1969:
2 CONT
2 CONT Fabian Chavez' mother dies
2 CONT
2 CONT Los Alamos (AP) - Mrs. Nicolasa Roybal de Chavez died at Los Alamos Medical Center Saturday after a short illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the mother of Fabian Chavez, who was the Democratic candidate for governor in last November's elections.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Albuquerque Journal of Sunday, Jan. 5, 1969:
2 CONT
2 CONT Fabian Chavez Mother Dies In Los Alamos
2 CONT
2 CONT Journal Special
2 CONT
2 CONT Los Alamos - The mother of former Democratic gubernatorial candidate Fabian Chavez, Mrs. Nicolasa Roybal de Chavez, died at the Los Alamos Medical Cener Saturday following a short illness. She was 84.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Chavez, who resided in New Mexico all her life and lived in Santa Fe since 1921, was preceded in death by her husband, Fabian Chavez, Sr., who died three years ago.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Wagon Mound in 1884, Mrs. Chavez attended Highlands University in Las Vegas and taught at Wagon Mound until 1909, when she was married. The family moved to Mora in 1916 when Chavez, Sr., was elected Mora County clerk.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family remained in Mora until 1921, when it moved to Santa Fe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Chavez is survived by
2 CONT *six sons
2 CONT **Friar Angelico Chavvez, Pena Blanca
2 CONT **Judge Rumaldo E. Chavez, Santa Fe;
2 CONT **Francisco E. Chavez, Los Alamos;
2 CONT **Fabian Chavez, Jr., Santa Fe;
2 CONT **Judge Antonio E. Chavez, Los Angeles; and
2 CONT **Jose A. C. Chavez of Santa Fe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also surviving are 
2 CONT *five daughters
2 CONT **Mrs. Vincent J. Matt, Los Angeles
2 CONT **Mrs. Nora Chavez, Santa Fe
2 CONT **Mrs. Alfonso Montoya, Los Angeles
2 CONT **Mrs. Norbert Gorski, Detroit; and
2 CONT **Mrs. Lorenzo Gutierrez of Santa Fe.
2 CONT
2 CONT A member of the Third Order of St. Francis and La Union Protectiva, Mrs. Chavez also is survived by:
2 CONT *two sisters
2 CONT **Mrs. A.A. Sosaya, and
2 CONT **Mrs. George King, both of Santa Fe; and
2 CONT *a brother, Tranquelino Roybal of Los Angeles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services are pending and will be announced by Memorial Chapel of Santa Fe.
