1 NOTE {geni:about_me} shares a 2nd great grandfather with husband, Juan Joseph Pacheco.
2 CONT
2 CONT I found My great-grandmother's Obituary Mary Delores (Dororita) Olivas, formerly Pacheco, Maiden Name Lebya, who passed on March 16th 1979. I retyped it exactly as written
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary for Mary Delores Olivas in the Santa Fe New Mexican Paper dated Sunday March 18 1979
2 CONT
2 CONT Olivas, Mary Delores, 73 A longtime Santa Cruz resident passed away at the Espanola Hospital Friday afternoon after a lengthy illness. Surviving her are her husband Julian Naguin Olivas of the home, four sons, Jose Narciso Pacheco
2 CONC  and wife, Eliza and Aldolfo Pacheco of Chacon. Frank Olivas and wife Cecelia of sombrillo, and Joe Olivas and wife, Barbara of Ulysses, Kan., five daughters, Cecelia Romero and Julie and husband, Ferminio Valdez of San Pedro, Dor
2 CONC a and husband Richard Garcia of El Guache, Mary and husband, Dave Miller of Florida, and Shonita Nelson of Washington, a stepson, Fred Olivas of Colorado, a son-in-law Robert O. Romero of Santa Cruz, a brother-in-law, Teresino Oli
2 CONC vas and wife, Carmen of Santa Cruz, several grand-children, great-grandchildren, nephews, and nieces, and many other relatives. Funeral arrangements are pending the arrival of relatives from out of state and will be announced late
2 CONC r by Block Salazar Morturary in Espanola.
2 CONT
2 CONT OLIVAS Mary Dolores —Correction of previous obituary  survived by husband Julian Maguin of the home in Santa Cruz. Also survived by two stepdaughters Mable Gonzales of Colorado and Charlotte Schramn of Omaha Nebraska and other rel
2 CONC atives. Devotional services will be held at  7:30 this evening at : Blocks-Salazar Mortuary Chapel in Espanola. Funeral Services are scheduled for 10:00 tomorrow morning from the United Methodist Church in Santa Cruz with Rev. Wil
2 CONC liam Martin officiating. Interment will follow in the Loma Vista Cemetery in Alcalde and surviving as active pallbearers will be Tommy Abeyta , Teresino Olivas, Danny Romero, Robert Romero, Joseph Pacheco, and Vidal Valdez. Honora
2 CONC ry named are Bobby Quintana, Rev. A.L. Brandstetter. Rev. Richard Campbell and Rev. William Martin. Blocks-Salazar Mortuary in Espanola. 
2 CONT
2 CONT note from my Aunt Brenda Nielson on 5/29/2013 I called mom and you are correct. His name is Fidel. His father was Juan ir John and his wife was Emelia. She didn't know her maiden name. Her mom was Dolores Leyba. Her mother died in
2 CONC  childbirth when she was born. She had an older brother and sister. Mom said that her sister had a funny old fashioned name.  Mom loved her and spent a lot of time with her family. They had 2 sons. Dolores father remarried and had
2 CONC  3 daughters. One of them was Laura. He left Dolores with a woman who raised her then later got her back but prob only to help with the children. Dolores may have been born in May.
