2 NOTE if she scolded me in spanish, I didn't understand her.  I corresponded with her in the '80's.  Her aide (Mary?) would translate and write for her.
2 NOTE lol lol she useto scold me for not knowing spanish, but then she would say its ok..
2 NOTE I remember that they were supposed to be salt free but sometimes she would add salt and enjoy them,  Afterwards her legs would hurt.
3 CONT
3 CONT And She loved when people would brush her hair.
3 CONT
3 CONT And one time, I made the mistake of asking her to speak english, Man did she chew me out!!!!!!!!!!!!!
3 CONT
3 CONT And the ant hills and the horned toads and the sunshine market and the Piggly Wiggly and.......................
2 NOTE MMMM yes and i remember she would add eggs to the dough when she was making it
2 NOTE Remember her tortillas were salt free? Nice warm memories of my great gramma
2 NOTE I remember Gramma.  She was soft and nice.  Too bad I didn't speak Spanish :(
2 NOTE I remember as lil' one once visited and played in an old home made pool... She made me eat the white part of the watermelon. She said it was good for me. lol...!
3 CONT Good times..!
2 NOTE Brought back memories, remembering going in the summer to visit and i would make tortillas with grandma celia.... good memories
