1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Decorated veteran of United States Army, WWII.   Purple Heart, Bronze Star, Bataan Medal, POW Medal.   Survived the Battle of Bataan in the Philippines 1941, captured by the Japanese Imperial Army at Corregidor in 
2 CONC May 1942.   Served as prisoner of war in the Philippines, Taiwan (Formosa), Manchuria, and Japan.  Middle son of nine children.  He owned several businesses, some with brother Ernesto (Erne) Terrazas, until retiring in 1975 for me
2 CONC dical reasons stemming from complications of military service.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Nick grew up in rural McKinley County, much of it on a farm in Bluewater.  He went to grade school and high school in Grants, NM.  He joined the army in 1941, and served in the 200th Coastal Artillery.  His unit was shipped to the
2 CONC  Philippines in 1941, then captured or destroyed there in the Battle of Bataan.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Nick had three brothers (Manuel, Constancio, Ernesto) and five sisters (Ofelia, Teofila, Carlota, Lucia, Margarita).  The siblings showed a mix of skin and eye coloration, with Manuel, Nick Ofelia and Margarita being very fair wit
2 CONC h light hair and eyes (like father Manuel), and Teofila, Carlota, Constancio, Lucia and Ernesto with swarthy skin and dark hair and eyes (like mother Candelaria).   
2 CONT
2 CONT When he was liberated from POW camp in Japan in 1945, his body weight was about half of what it had been before the war, and he had contracted a variety of diseases, including malaria and beriberi.  Army doctors did not think he w
2 CONC ould survive long.   He met Evangeline Otero in 1946. They married and had three children, only one of whom (Ronald) survived.   He and Evangeline divorced in 1958.  Nick later married Sadie Garcia, with whom they had a daughter, 
2 CONC Judith Ann.   
