1 NAME Angela L. /Sosaya/
2 GIVN Angela L.
2 SURN Sosaya
2 _MARNM Biddle
2 NICK Angelina
2 NICK Angie
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Rosario Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Santa Fe
3 STAE New Mexico
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 14 OCT 1910
2 ADDR
3 CITY Santa Fe
3 STAE New Mexico Territory
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 4 JUN 2002
2 PLAC Home of her sister and brother-in-law
2 ADDR
3 CITY Santa Fe
3 STAE New Mexico
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Model for Russian artist Leon Gaspard, fashion designer, employee for St. Vincent Hospital
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the tribute given her by Tom Udall in the Congressional Record:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Sosaya&GSiman=1&GScid=38372&GRid=38617016&
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.gpo.gov/fdsys/pkg/CREC-2002-06-07/html/CREC-2002-06-07-pt1-PgE987-4.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Angie was known as one of Santa Fe's most wonderful and lively characters. Angie was a common sight to many clothing stores and people along the Plaza and Acequia Madre Street. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She loved to visit with store owners and discuss the latest fashions. Angie had worked with clothing designer Agnes James and at Suzette's at the La Fonda Hotel. While working for Agnes James, Angie designed the Buffalo Hunter shi
2 CONC rt and the Bustle-Back broomstick skirt. Her sister, Stella Montoya, continues to still use the original patterns.
2 CONT
2 CONT In her twenties, Angie enjoyed going out with the crew of the movie Santa Fe Trail. Her beauty was well known, and she was often used as a model by many of Santa Fe artists in the 1930's and 1940's. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Angie enjoyed regaling her family with stories of when she and her cousin Fray Angelico Chavez were young, and would accompany her parents on the long drives to Albuquerque. She would tell how she and Fray Angelico often found it 
2 CONC necessary to get out of the car and help to push it over La Bajada Hill.
2 CONT
2 CONT Throughout her life Angie remained interested in fashions and kept that desire burning in her sisters and nieces. She always let her nieces know that they could wear pearls at anytime and with anything, and many of them still wear
2 CONC  their pearls just that way. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Angie had a love for anything French and had enjoyed her visits to France. The first time she traveled to Europe was with her mother aboard the Queen Mary. She was often seen at this French Pastry Shop at the La Fonda Hotel, where
2 CONC  she loved to indulge in the crepes. She also loved to drive her ‘‘French'' cars—her Renault and her beloved Peugeot.
2 CONT
2 CONT While her nieces and nephews attended Acequia Madre elementary school, Angie would be a common sight, always stopping by to bring them treats and small gifts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in 1910 to Augustin and Victoria Sosaya, she was preceded in death by 
2 CONT *her parents, 
2 CONT *her sisters, 
2 CONT **Mary, 
2 CONT **Consuelo, 
2 CONT **Delores,and 
2 CONT **Florence, 
2 CONT *her husband Martin Biddle, and 
2 CONT *her son Michael Biddle. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by 
2 CONT *sisters 
2 CONT **Anita Nelson, of California, 
2 CONT **Stella Montoya and husband Eloy, 
2 CONT **Monica Sosaya Halford and husband Richard, of Santa Fe, and 
2 CONT *her brother Augustin Sosaya and wife Priscilla, of California. 
2 CONT *Numerous nieces and nephews also survive her.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From her Obituary:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.genlookups.com/nm/webbbs_config.pl/noframes/read/499
2 CONT
2 CONT ANGELA SOSAYA BIDDLE, 91, of Santa Fe, died Tuesday at the home of her sister and brother-in-law. She was born in Santa Fe Oct. 14, 1910. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She enjoyed notoriety as a model to the late Russian artist Leon Gaspard in Taos. She served as a designer for Agnes James at Santa Fe's Pins and Needles, and she was formerly employed at St. Vincent Hospital. For the majority of 
2 CONC her life, she remained a member of Cristo Rey parish. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by 
2 CONT *her parents, Agustin Sr. and Victoria Roybal Sosaya; 
2 CONT *husband, Martin 'Jack' Biddle; 
2 CONT *son, Michael Biddle; and 
2 CONT *three sisters, 
2 CONT **Florence Conley, 
2 CONT **Mary Dolores Sosaya and 
2 CONT **Consuelo Sosaya. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by 
2 CONT *Anita (the late Harry) Nelson of Alamo, Calif.; 
2 CONT *Stella (Eloy) Montoya of Santa Fe; 
2 CONT *Agustin (Priscilla) Sosaya Jr. of La Mesa, Calif.; 
2 CONT *Monica (Richard Sr.) Halford of Santa Fe; and 
2 CONT *many nieces and nephews. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A rosary will be recited at 7 p.m. today at Cristo Rey Catholic Church. Mass will be celebrated at 10 a.m. Saturday at Cristo Rey Church. Santa Fe Funeral Options.
