0 @N6000000002279602890@ NOTE Colorado Marriage License # 1040.
1 CONT Marriage Padrinos: Actonino? Martines and Ines? Apodaca
1 CONT
1 CONT The census of 1880 shows Felipe Mestas living with his parents and four brothers and sisters east of Trinidad in Chililicito. The Mestas family lived close to Nicolasa Fernandez, so it is quite probable that the families knew each
1 CONC  other. Other than the census, I have no documentation on Felipe though I have searched for it. Family stories indicate he worked at the court house in Trinidad as a translator. Supposedly, he owned land in Chililicito, though I d
1 CONC oubt it. Because after his death Eloisa and their two daughters lived in poverty. By 1900, the census shows Eloisa to be widowed; that makes Felipe dead by age 33. We are told he died of alcoholism; it would be interesting to see 
1 CONC a death certificate to see if in fact that is true. 
1 CONT Source: Information from an unknown (Family Tree Maker) family tree contributor as posted on Ancestry.com, date unknown. 
