0 @N6000000002279598064@ NOTE Baptized May 7, 1898, Trinidad, Colorado.
1 CONT Padrinos: Refugio Sanchiz and Maria Concepcion de Sanchiz (Torres).
1 CONT Silverio didn't like to have pictures taken of him.
1 CONT Silverio and Fructosa Mestas were godparents to "Silver Gurule" who was named after Silverio.
1 CONT Silverio and his wife Fructosa used to listen to "Eddie Arnold", country western music,  from Dalhart, Texas and World War II news, when their son Daniel was in the war overseas, on the family radio.
1 CONT This radio, now an antique, has been passed on to Daniel Mestas's son Orlando.
1 CONT Silverio worked as ranch hand and laborer at the Ernest G. Myers Ranch in Hoehne, Colorado along with his brother Salvador Mestas where he worked from December 1922 until March 1947 just shortly before his death.
1 CONT Exempt from World War I due to "Sole Provider Status".
1 CONT Buried: August 26, 1947, Hoehne Cemetery, Hoehne, Colorado and is buried next to his sister Altagracia Mestas Montoya who died in 1960.
1 CONT Silverio died at the home of his son Daniel Mestas at 517 Convent Street, Trinidad, Colorado when he was 49 years, 4 months and 19 days old.  Death was due to Cerebral Hemorrhage, Arteriosclerosis.
1 CONT Had been ill since February of 1947.
0 @N6000000002279598210@ NOTE Baptized on June 15, 1882.
1 CONT Padrinos: Diego Lusero and Maria Francisita Baca de Torrez.
1 CONT Marriage padrinos: Manuel Garcia and Maria Pedra de Armenta.
1 CONT Handwritten note by Altagracia Mestas indicates that the Mestas Family came from Chama, New Mexico arriving in Las Animas County, Colorado on April 15, 1866.
1 CONT
1 CONT Altagracia died at the age of 78  at Mount San Rafael Hospital, Trinidad, Colorado and was a life-long resident of Las Animas County, Colorado.
1 CONT
1 CONT Funeral services were held at Holy Family Catholic Church, Hoehne, Colorado
1 CONT Buried: Hoehne Cemetery next to her brother Silverio Mestas.
0 @N6000000002279598221@ NOTE Baptized on August 16, 1884.
1 CONT Padrinos: Juan Borse and Maria Concepcion Tenorio.
1 CONT Died at the home of his parents near Hoehne, Colorado.
1 CONT Death due to inflammation of the kidneys
1 CONT Buried on April 24, 1903 in the Hoehne Cemetery.
1 CONT Daniel was 19 years, 8 months and 17 days at the time of his death.
0 @N6000000002279598232@ NOTE Baptized on September 23, 1888, Trinidad, Colorado.
1 CONT Padrinos: Querino Abeyta and Maria Donaciana de Martines.
1 CONT State of new Mexico Marriage License #0948.
1 CONT Marriage Witnesses: Pedro Valdez and Adelaida Valdez
1 CONT Affectionately called "Pa Toto" by his family.
1 CONT Buried at Fairmount Cemetery, Raton, New Mexico.
0 @N6000000002279598243@ NOTE Baptized: December 16, 1890 in Trinidad, Colorado.
1 CONT Padrinos: Maria Rita Ribera and Juan Aliris.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage Padrinos: Jesus Baca and Ana Mitchell.
1 CONT
1 CONT Killed during an explosion that occured at 2:00 in the afternoon at the Dupont-DeNemours Powder Company in Augusta, Colorado (near Aguilar, Colorado).  
1 CONT Cornelio had started working at the powder plant the day before the explosion occured and was living in Augusta at the time of his death.
1 CONT Verdict Of Jury from an inquest held in Augusta, Colorado on July 7, 1917.
1 CONT That the above named (including C.C. Mestas) came to thir death at about 2:00 P.M. June 29, 1917 at the plant of the Dupont Powder Company at Augusta, Colorado from an explosion in the press and coining room.  From the evidence pr
1 CONC oduced we believe that the explosion was from some accidental cause unkown to this jury.  We further find that there was no neglect on the part of the company.
1 CONT
1 CONT Buried in Aguilar, Colorado. (Exact location unknown)
0 @N6000000002279598254@ NOTE Baptized: May 8, 1893, Trinidad, Colorado.
