0 @N6000000002279598275@ NOTE Baptized January 19, 1896, Trinidad, Colorado.
1 CONT Padrinos: Juan Pablo Gallegos and Maria Crucita de Gallegos.
1 CONT a.k.a. Uncle Pete.
1 CONT Lived with his sister Altagracia after her husband Leonardo Montoya died.
1 CONT Served in World War I.
1 CONT Dressed like a cowboy and worked for Ernest Myers Ranch with his brother Silverio Mestas in Hoehne, Colorado.  He was good at breaking horses and worked as a ranch hand.
1 CONT Salvador also worked at Vermijo Park near Trinidad.
1 CONT Divorced from Luisa Olguin in March 1929.
1 CONT Died at Mt. San Rafael Hospital, Trinidad, Colorado at 10:30 AM and is buried in the Trinidad Catholic Cemetery.
1 CONT Salvador has a military headstone.
0 @N6000000002279603545@ NOTE Baptized: October 4, 1886.
1 CONT Padrinos: Trinidad Martinez and Dorotea Mestas.
0 @N6000000002279603655@ NOTE Died of Typhoid Fever.
