1 CONT Buried in Mestas and Elkins Cemetery.
0 @N6000000002279616123@ NOTE Please see the Montoya Family Heritage for the full genealogy of Andreita and her husband Jose Igancio Montoya's family lineage.
1 CONT Andreita's father Trinidad Martinez was buried in the El Ojito Cemetery near Hoehne, Colorado.
1 CONT Andreita was buried in the Trinidad Catholic Cemetery, Trinidad, Colorado.
0 @N6000000002279631522@ NOTE Baptized on May 21, 1893 in Trinidad, Colorado.
1 CONT
1 CONT Colorado Marriage License #1267.
1 CONT Marriage Padrinos: Guillermo Lopez and Maria Mestas.
1 CONT
1 CONT Nicolasa Julia, named for her grandmother but used the name Julia, was the  first daughter born to Felipe Mestas and Eloisa Jaramillo. She married Louis G. Mendez and they had four children. They later divorced but remained friend
1 CONC s till their death. Julia moved to Denver in the 1940's and operated A & M Cleaners with the help of her daughters. Her daughters have told me that she was a wonderful mother, a superior cook and seamstress and a good woman  who w
1 CONC as always willing to help her family and extended family in time of need. She died of heart disease in 1968 and is buried at Mt. Olivet in Denver.
1 CONT As told to me by her daughters Helen and Carmen. 
1 CONT Source: Information from an unknown (Family Tree Maker) family tree contributor as posted on Ancestry.com, date unknown.
1 CONT
1 CONT Buried in 1968 at Mount Olivet Cemetery, Denver, Colorado.
0 @N6000000002279631533@ NOTE Baptized on April 21, 1896 in Trinidad, Colorado.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage Padrinos: Andres Sope and Doloritas Martinez.
1 CONT
1 CONT Maria, AKA Mary, was the second and last child born to Eloisa Jaramillo Mestas. In 1922, she married Jose N. Trujillo. Together they had four children. They ran the Denver Hotel in the 200 block of N. Commercial St. in Trinidad du
1 CONC ring the 1940's. They also lived in Walsenburg, CO. They weren't too close to family members for whatever reason. She did not even list her mother's name on her marriage document. In 1952, Jose died and she moved to NM. I heard th
1 CONC at she remarried and was later killed in an automobile accident in Talpa, NM. 
1 CONT Source: Information from an unknown (Family Tree Maker) family tree contributor as posted on Ancestry.com, date unknown. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Buried in Taos, New Mexico.
0 @N6000000002279619779@ NOTE Colorado Marriage License #2296.
0 @N6000000002279598008@ NOTE Baptized: October 10, 1920, Hoehne, Colorado by the Rev. J.B. Hugh, S.J.
1 CONT Padrinos: John Watson and Emma T. Watson.
1 CONT
1 CONT Served in World War II as part of the Army's 42nd Rainbow Division, Battery B, 402nd Field Artillery that was instrumental in the liberation of the Dachau Concentration Camp in Munich, Germany.
1 CONT Known as Danny Mestas in the military due to his registering for the military under the name Danny instead of Daniel.
1 CONT Danny was stationed at Camp Gruber, Oklahoma at one time during his military service.
1 CONT Daniel received his High School Diploma after returning from military service on December 30, 1949 in Hoehne, Colorado.
1 CONT
1 CONT Married at Holy Trinity Catholic Church in Trinidad.
1 CONT Marriage Padrinos: Joe Max Lopez and Geneva (Sanchez) Lopez (Corina Sanchez's sister).
1 CONT Living at 1004 East First in Trinidad, Colorado at the time of his marriage.
1 CONT Daniel and Corina were living at 707 Elizabeth in Pueblo, Colorado at the time of the birth of their second son Daniel Phillip on June 4, 1955.
1 CONT Daniel was employed at the Pueblo Army Depot as a mechanical/electrical repair technician for 26 years.
1 CONT Was living at 111 South 3rd Street, LaSalle, Colorado where he died from Progressive Supranuclear Palsy at the age of 78 years.
1 CONT Buried: Imperial Memorial Gardens, 5450 Highway 78 West Pueblo, Pueblo, Colorado, 81005 with his wife Corina M. (Sanchez) Mestas.
0 @N6000000002279598086@ NOTE Left Hoehne, Colorado by 1940 to start work at Mt. San Rafael Hospital in Trinidad, Colorado.
1 CONT Lived on 619 Baltic St., Colorado Springs, Colorado, at one time, as indicated on her Social Security card.
1 CONT Gertrude was the Mestas and Montoya family member who was considered to be the historian of the family.  Along with her written accounts, she was also the person that everyone would told to ask a family related question of because
1 CONC  she seemed to know, all their was to know, about the family's  relationships, stories and events that made up the Mestas and Montoya's family history.  
1 CONT Buried:Trinidad Catholic Cemetery, Trinidad, Colorado near her mother Fructosa Mestas.
1 CONT Lived at 117 Benedicta Avenue, Trinidad, Colorado at the time of her death with her daughter Alice Vasquez.
0 @N6000000002279598097@ NOTE Padrino: Maseimo Martinez.
1 CONT Died in Hoehne, at the home of her parents, when she was five years old from some type of insect bite.
1 CONT The night before she died she was eating pinon nuts with her father Silverio Mestas.
1 CONT Funeral was held at the family residence, at 10:00 in the morning on Oct. 3, 1927, with burial in the "El Ojito" cemetery.
1 CONT Campbell Lewis Mortuary was in charge of arrangements.
0 @N6000000002279598108@ NOTE Baptized June 15, 1924.
1 CONT Padrinos: Francisco Hernandes and Maria Ignacia Bustos de Hernandes.
1 CONT Died from pneumonia.
0 @N6000000002279598119@ NOTE Baptized: July 7, 1929, Trinidad, Colorado.
1 CONT Padrinos: Jose Duran and Paula Olguin.
1 CONT Confirmed: October 18, 1942, Trinidad.
1 CONT Alejandro Mestas and Alex "Shorty" Watson (cousins) were both baptized on the same day and both given the name Alejandro.
1 CONT Juan and Virginia Lujan were godparents of Alejandro Mestas.
1 CONT Served in the Korean War as a Seargent. Enlisted January 12, 1949-52.
1 CONT U.S. Army Ground Forces
1 CONT 48th F.A. BN. 7th Inf. Div. Service Battery.
1 CONT Serial No# 17263166
1 CONT See Las Animas County Korean War Memorial in Trinidad, Colorado.
0 @N6000000002279598607@ NOTE Baptized on April 21, 1912.
1 CONT Padrinos: Albino de Blanche and Teofila Pacheco.
1 CONT Buried: Garcia Cemetery located east of Trinidad, Colorado not far from the Catholic Cemetery.
0 @N6000000002279598922@ NOTE Baptized: April 20, 1905, Trinidad, Colorado.
1 CONT Padrinos: Jose Miguel Brito and Maria Martinez.
1 CONT Verdict Of Jury from an Inquisition held on February 5, 1931 in Trinidad, Colorado. 
1 CONT That Joe N. Montoya came to his death at Mount San Rafael Hospital, Trinidad, Colorado, County of Las Animas on February 2, 1931.  Cause of death was Pneumonia which developed following a bullet wound in the abdomen.  Said wound w
1 CONC as inflicted by a pistol in the hands of Filiberto Vigil.  Said shooting occured January 29, 1931 near Hoehne, Colorado, County of Las Animas.  We the jury in this case find that death was caused by accidental shooting.  
1 CONT Filiberto Vigil worked for Mike Trujillo who was a first cousin to Sotelo Martinez  the father of Mandye Martinez who later married Art Sandoval.  Mike Trujillo was married to Cruzita an aunt of Art Sandoval's. 
0 @N6000000002279598933@ NOTE Baptized: August 24, 1907, Hoehne, Colorado.
1 CONT Padrinos: Jose Ignacio Montoya and Maria Gertrudes Salazar de Montoya.
1 CONT Believed to have died from Spinal Meningitis.
1 CONT Buried at the Mestas Cemetery near Hoehne, Colorado.
0 @N6000000002279598637@ NOTE Affectionately called "Tia B" by her family. 
1 CONT  "Flor De Las Flores"
1 CONT Raised in Barela Mesa, New Mexico where she loved to camp out and help on the ranch raising pigs, gardening and working with the cows.
1 CONT "I can't remember if we were poor or what just because we layered the walls with Denver Post newspapers instead of using paint".
1 CONT Beatrice had 10 children, 35 Grandchildren, 58 Great-grandchildren and 4 Great-great grandchildren (107) at the time of her death.
1 CONT Buried in Fairmont Cemetery, Raton, New Mexico.
0 @N6000000002279598648@ NOTE Her patron saint was Santo Nino de Atocha.
1 CONT Buried in Fairmont Cemetery, Raton, New Mexico.
1 CONT Ofelia had 21 grandchildren, 37 great grandchildren and 9 great-great grandchildren.
