0 @N6000000002279598694@ NOTE a.k.a. Freddie Mestas
1 CONT He was the second son of Salvadore and Luisa Mestas.  Their first son Socorro died young.
1 CONT Baptized on October 11, 1931.
1 CONT Padrinos: Davel Trujillo and Anna Trujillo.
1 CONT Confirmed: Model, Colorado, August 21, 1949.
1 CONT John Alfred and Aurora owned land along the river bottom near Hoehne that was the original homestead of Jose Freyta who was married to Susana Montoya.
1 CONT After the separation of his parents (Salvador and Luisa) John Alfred was raised by the Pedro and Estanislada Olguin.
1 CONT Freddie lived for awhile (in the bunk house) at Tony Garcia's residence. Tony was a son-in-law to the Olguin family.
1 CONT Tony supported Freddie through his first year and a half of high school.
1 CONT Freddie said Mestas' were originally from Greece.
1 CONT Freddie was known to have a Mestas Journal that has extensive information on the Mestas family.  The book was handed down to his dad (Salvador Mestas) from his sister Altagracia and given to Alfredo.
1 CONT Served in the U.S. Navy (UT1) during the Korean War.
1 CONT Buried in Trinidad, Colorado, 81082, at the Trinidad Catholic Cemetery.
1 CONT Freddie resided at 5227 Alta Loma Rd., Colorado Springs, Colorado at the time of his death.
